The test `['org.apache.commons.cli2.bug.BugCLI123Test.testSingleChildOption()']` failed.
The test looks like:

```java
80 :     public void testSingleChildOption() throws OptionException {
81 :         CommandLine cl = parser.parse(new String[] { "--child", "test" });
86 :     }
```

Current bug report: {'summary': 'the minimum and maximum constraints on a group do not take other groups into account', 'description': "If you have a Group A as a child of Group B and you set a minimum or maximum on Group B, the presence or not of Group A will not affect GroupB. This is because Groups are never added to a CommandLine so .hasOption(A) returns false and so it isn't counted. WriteableCommandLine#addOption(Option) should be used to indicate that a Group is present if any of a Groups children is present.\n"}

Proceed to fault localisation and produce a step-by-step diagnosis.

